    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="0843" n="835" xml:id="pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/917: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Erwin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-19T15:00:00-05:00">November 19, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Your 30, November 18, 11 a.m. Please advise the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    that the interest of his Government in the refugee problem and his desire that
                    Honduran policy shall conform to that of the United States is greatly
                    appreciated. You should continue along the following lines:</p>
                <p>The United States is now admitting from Germany approximately 27,000 persons per
                    annum, without regard to race or religious belief, the maximum number permitted
                    by law. It is at the same time considering what other possible contribution it
                    can make to the solution of this problem, which the latest wave of persecution
                    in Germany has made urgent in the extreme. It is hoped that the Government of
                    Honduras will actively consider on broad humanitarian lines what contribution it
                    can make to a solution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
